\begin_layout Abstract
This report reconstructs the four-machine, ten-bus, two-area system in Padiyar, 
\emph on
Power System Dynamics: Stability and Control
\emph default
, second edition, Section
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

9.6.1. Tables
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

9.1–9.4 are treated as the primary input source. Each generator uses Padiyar model
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

1.1, a two-axis transient synchronous-machine model, with either manual excitation or the printed single-time-constant AVR. The AVR case has five states per generator and twenty states in total. The in-house Newton–Raphson power flow, DAE equilibrium, small-signal linearisation and implicit-trapezoidal transient simulation are generated from project code. Table
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

9.5 is used only as a secondary published cross-check; no parameter is fitted to its eigenvalues. 
\end_layout

