\begin_layout Section
Power-flow analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The project-owned Newton–Raphson solver uses bus
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

11 as the reference bus, matching the zero angle printed in Table
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

9.2. Buses 1, 2 and 12 are PV buses. Line susceptance 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset

 from Table
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset

9.1 is represented as 
\begin_inset Formula $B/2$
\end_inset

 at each end of the standard 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi$
\end_inset

 model. This convention reproduces the printed operating point.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Newton–Raphson formulation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The solver iterates on the polar voltage state 
\begin_inset Formula $x=[\theta_2,\ldots,\theta_N,\,
|V|_{PQ_1},\ldots]^T$
\end_inset

 (slack angle fixed, PV magnitudes fixed). Bus power injections are computed from the admittance matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $Y=G+jB$
\end_inset

: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align}
P_i(x) &= |V_i|\sum_{j=1}^{N}|V_j|\bigl(G_{ij}\cos\theta_{ij}+B_{ij}\sin\theta_{ij}\bigr),\\
Q_i(x) &= |V_i|\sum_{j=1}^{N}|V_j|\bigl(G_{ij}\sin\theta_{ij}-B_{ij}\cos\theta_{ij}\bigr),
\end{align}
\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{ij}=\theta_i-\theta_j$
\end_inset

. The power mismatch is 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta P_i=P_i^{\text{spec}}-P_i(x)$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta Q_i=Q_i^{\text{spec}}-Q_i(x)$
\end_inset

. At each iteration the Newton step solves 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
J(x_k)\,\Delta x = \begin{bmatrix}\Delta P\\ \Delta Q\end{bmatrix},
\qquad x_{k+1}=x_k+\Delta x,
\end{equation}
\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $J$
\end_inset

 is the standard 
\begin_inset Formula $4$
\end_inset

-block Jacobian with sub-matrices 
\begin_inset Formula $H=\partial P/\partial\theta$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $N=\partial P/\partial|V|$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $M=\partial Q/\partial\theta$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $L=\partial Q/\partial|V|$
\end_inset

. Iteration terminates when 
\begin_inset Formula $\max|\Delta P,\Delta Q|<10^{-10}$
\end_inset

. No external nonlinear solver is used; the Jacobian is built analytically from
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $Y$
\end_inset

 in project code.
\end_layout

